        "narration": "Candles were lit at noon across New England. On May 19, 1780, daylight vanished completely without warning.",
        "visual_keywords": "dark foggy countryside town"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Roosters roosted, cattle retreated to barns, and terrified crowds filled churches, believing Judgment Day had arrived.",
        "visual_keywords": "old wooden church interior"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Black soot rained from the sky, yet no local fires were burning. What could blot out the sun across five colonies?",
        "visual_keywords": "rain falling dark woods"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Tree ring analysis in Canada finally revealed the cause: massive forest fires in Ontario sent an enormous soot cloud into the upper atmosphere.",
        "visual_keywords": "close up tree rings"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Driven by high winds, that giant soot blanket blocked the sun, turning wildfire smoke into an apocalyptic legend.",
        "visual_keywords": "sun breaking through smoke"
      }
